<title>PERU: SOCCER-PERU BEAT CHILE 2-1 IN WORLD CUP QUALIFIER.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-PERU BEAT CHILE 2-1 IN WORLD CUP QUALIFIER.</headline>
<dateline>LIMA 1997-01-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Peru beat Chile 2-1 (halftime 2-0)</p>
<p>in a South American World Cup soccer qualifying match on</p>
<p>Sunday.</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Peru - Flavio Maestri (14th minute), Roberto Palacios</p>
<p>(34th)</p>
<p>Chile - Ivan Zamorano (88th)</p>
<p>Standings (tabulate under played, won, drawn, lost, goals</p>
<p>for, goals against, points)</p>
<p> Colombia     7  5  2  0  14  5 17</p>
<p> Paraguay     7  4  2  1   8  3 14</p>
<p> Argentina    7  2  4  1  10  7 10</p>
<p> Uruguay	7  3  1  3   6  6 10</p>
<p> Bolivia	7  2  3  2  11  7  9</p>
<p> Ecuador	7  3  0  4   8  9  9</p>
<p> Peru	   7  2  3  2   8  9  9</p>
<p> Chile	  7  2  2  3  10 11  8</p>
<p> Venezuela    8  0  1  7   5 23  1</p>
<p>Note: top four teams qualify for the 1998 World Cup in</p>
<p>France. Brazil qualify automatically as holders.</p>
</text>
